# SHContent DevOps

**Production:** https://workflow.sherifharidyjewelry.com · **Health:** `GET /api/health`  
**VPS:** `/opt/shcontent` · **Secrets:** `/etc/shcontent/.env` (never commit)

## Compose project name

The stack **must** use `name: shcontent` in `deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml`.  
Never deploy from a bare `deploy/` folder without an explicit project name — it defaults to `deploy` and collides with SHFlow.

Containers: `shcontent-api-1`, `shcontent-web-1`, `shcontent-postgres-1`. Database: Postgres (same pattern as SHFlow).

## Deploy

Always pass `--env-file /etc/shcontent/.env` so `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` matches between the Postgres container and API `DATABASE_URL`.

```bash
cd web && npm ci && npm run build
rsync -avz --exclude .git --exclude web/node_modules --exclude .env ./ root@72.62.51.230:/opt/shcontent/
rsync -avz --delete web/dist/ root@72.62.51.230:/opt/shcontent/web/dist/
ssh root@72.62.51.230 "chmod -R a+rX /opt/shcontent/web/dist && cd /opt/shcontent/deploy && docker compose --env-file /etc/shcontent/.env -f docker-compose.prod.yml -f docker-compose.domains.yml up -d --build"
```

If Postgres auth fails after a password change, reset the volume (pre-prod):  
`docker volume rm deploy_shcontent_pgdata` then redeploy.

Canonical guide: `sh-ops` repo → `docs/DEVOPS.md`, `docs/DEPLOYMENT_SETUP.md`.
